# Line endings are LF everywhere — in the index and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) rewrites every checked-out file to
# CRLF while Prettier's `endOfLine` defaults to `lf`. The result is that a fresh clone fails
# `npm run format:check` on code nobody has touched, and every file a contributor *does* touch
# reports a modification whose diff is empty. CI never sees it, because Linux checks out LF.
#
# The index is already LF throughout, so this changes only what checkout writes — no
# renormalisation is needed, and running one would produce a whole-repo diff for nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated by npm and never merged by hand
package-lock.json -diff
